.cursorrules
# Project Rules & Coding Standards

## 1. Paradigm & Structure (STRICT)
- ALL code must follow strict Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) principles.
- Use Classes for modules (e.g., `CodeParser`, `DiagramRenderer`, `HistoryManager`, `FirestoreSync`).
- Use Interfaces/Types for data structures.
- Encapsulate logic; strictly avoid global variables and spaghetti functions.

## 2. Backend & Firestore (STRICT)
- DO NOT use n8n, Docker, or any external backend servers. 
- USE EXCLUSIVELY Firebase/Firestore for data persistence and Cloud Functions if server logic is needed.
- Firestore Security Rules and Paths must strictly use EVEN path segments (e.g., `users/{userId}/diagrams/{diagramId}`). NEVER use odd segments for document references to prevent "invalid argument" errors.

## 3. PWA & Offline-First
- A valid `manifest.json` and robust Service Workers are mandatory.
- Implement IndexedDB for local data storage. The app MUST perform all CRUD operations on IndexedDB first, then sync to Firestore in the background when online.
- Diagram parsing and rendering must happen 100% client-side.

## 4. Refactoring Rule
- When prompting an AI for modifications or refactoring, you MUST include: "Respeta la estructura actual de la app dictada en las .cursorrules". Do not break OOP structure or offline capabilities.

## 5. Version Control
- Commit changes incrementally using Git. Meaningful commit messages are required.